    "display_title": "chore(ci): the digests compare each set with the base's, not only engine with engine",
    "event": "pull_request",
    "head_branch": "chore/digests-against-main",
    "head_commit_message": "chore(ci): the digests compare each set with the base's, not only engine with engine\n\nThe digest jobs compared a branch's two engines with each other, so an\noutcome change both engines share passed. Each digest job now takes the\nbase's GDScript digest of its set from a worktree of the merge base and\ncompares it tick by tick (check_outcomes.py). A branch that means to\nchange outcomes says why in an `Outcomes-changed: <why>` trailer on any\nof its commits; without one, a changed run fails the job and is named\nwith its first differing tick. The SUMMARY prints each set's verdict.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PQFXanRmU4gRu8h9tLwpwp",
